    },
    {
      "id": "stIHBdK-RHesWwVTdFtDp",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -542.1022665351566,
      "y": 2566.3702238108717,
      "width": 729.1797485351562,
      "height": 180,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "az",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 681549164,
      "version": 352,
      "versionNonce": 431691220,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1774118686084,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "* Need to use a Layer 4 load balancer.\n* Since the chat server is stateful, and \n   needs to maintain live connection,\n* Cannot have network (L7) load balancer",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "* Need to use a Layer 4 load balancer.\n* Since the chat server is stateful, and \n   needs to maintain live connection,\n* Cannot have network (L7) load balancer",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "KeS1BTZgqlYNzlrycdPeo",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -865.2342289162219,
      "y": 3704.946349095093,
      "width": 2697.69482421875,
      "height": 720,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b00",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1960081492,
      "version": 1439,
      "versionNonce": 1659579348,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1774158364047,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Whatsapp famously served 2 million users per server, with modern hardwares, it can be even more. \n\nBut, when the scale increases, and we have multiple chat servers to handle. Since this chat servers are not stateless, we need to know, which client has \nestablished connection with which server, so that connections can be used to send messages over the websockets.\nIt breaks the 1st NFR - \"delivered with low-latency < 500 ms.\"\n\nCurrent data flow:\n1. user A -> drops message.\n2. message reached chatServer 1.\n3. chatServer 1 writes to Messages and Inbox tables.\n4. chatServer 1 now needs to send the message to User B (intended target for the message).\n5. Connection to User B is already established by chatServer 2. \n6. Asking chatServer 1 will breadk the 1st NFR to get the messages delivered with low latency.\n7. We need a mechanism so chatServer 1 can identify which chatServer has already established connection with user B.\n\n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Whatsapp famously served 2 million users per server, with modern hardwares, it can be even more. \n\nBut, when the scale increases, and we have multiple chat servers to handle. Since this chat servers are not stateless, we need to know, which client has \nestablished connection with which server, so that connections can be used to send messages over the websockets.\nIt breaks the 1st NFR - \"delivered with low-latency < 500 ms.\"\n\nCurrent data flow:\n1. user A -> drops message.\n2. message reached chatServer 1.\n3. chatServer 1 writes to Messages and Inbox tables.\n4. chatServer 1 now needs to send the message to User B (intended target for the message).\n5. Connection to User B is already established by chatServer 2. \n6. Asking chatServer 1 will breadk the 1st NFR to get the messages delivered with low latency.\n7. We need a mechanism so chatServer 1 can identify which chatServer has already established connection with user B.\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
