    {
      "id": "CXvTs0KvX2GfSpjWHoRMV",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1637.4462798054615,
      "y": 4478.3215750527115,
      "width": 521.495849609375,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1S",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 618304364,
      "version": 270,
      "versionNonce": 1088481364,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1774162037439,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Data flow:\n-------------\n- create a topic per user.\n- write to the user's topic \nwhen a msg needs to be sent.",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Data flow:\n-------------\n- create a topic per user.\n- write to the user's topic \nwhen a msg needs to be sent.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "0lFd65Uli67tySBdyeutY",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 951.9730944726365,
      "y": 7110.564918871199,
      "width": 1737.79150390625,
      "height": 585,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1T",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 623916116,
      "version": 1234,
      "versionNonce": 1623144404,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1774162043389,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\n\n\nAgain, Not a very good solution, causes issues during scaling.\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------\nConsistent hashing ring algorithm will make sure, most of the users will stay on their server.\nbut 20% of them will have to change (proved in the algo's paper), since the new server will\noverlap somewhat with the previous server.\nThis connection reset has to be done slowly, so there's not a lot of them reconnections happening\nsimultaneously.\n\nIn this case, when the transition is happening, we need to maybe route the message to 2 servers,\nsince the userB can be connected to any 1 of them.",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\n\n\nAgain, Not a very good solution, causes issues during scaling.\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------\nConsistent hashing ring algorithm will make sure, most of the users will stay on their server.\nbut 20% of them will have to change (proved in the algo's paper), since the new server will\noverlap somewhat with the previous server.\nThis connection reset has to be done slowly, so there's not a lot of them reconnections happening\nsimultaneously.\n\nIn this case, when the transition is happening, we need to maybe route the message to 2 servers,\nsince the userB can be connected to any 1 of them.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "AAUvrLRlzwdw7e-SGU9qD",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1210.7470896584414,
      "y": 5034.56293895465,
      "width": 1689.0836181640625,
      "height": 945,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1U",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1316829140,
      "version": 2188,
      "versionNonce": 1455996372,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1774162037439,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Option C: Redis Pub/Sub (best option, but not panacea, has it's own problems)\n[acts as data plane]\n--------------------------------\nSolution approach used in kafka is the right approach, but with wrong technology.\nhow is works is - as a chatServer, you can tell Redis, i want to listen to this particular\ntopic (in this case, 1 user as 1 topic). \nWhen a message is dropped by userA to serverA, it'll drop that message to redis.\nRedis sees, who's subscribed to the topic, and sends them the message.\n\n                          Limitations\n                          --------------\n                          - Redis pubsub offers, atmost once delivery of messages, \n                            which is pretty bad, but is ok  for us, since we already have a \n                            fault tolerant mechanism in the Inbox table.\n                          \n                          - Since the Redis is part of the data plane, it needs to scale and\nhandle the distributed traffic. Now, as redis scales, each of the chat server needs to have\nconnection with every redis server (NXM connections).\nIn this case, the redis cluster is not doing a lot, just passing along messageIds. \nIf the system scales to trillions of users, it might become an issue for us, since the numbers of\nconnections to explode.",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Option C: Redis Pub/Sub (best option, but not panacea, has it's own problems)\n[acts as data plane]\n--------------------------------\nSolution approach used in kafka is the right approach, but with wrong technology.\nhow is works is - as a chatServer, you can tell Redis, i want to listen to this particular\ntopic (in this case, 1 user as 1 topic). \nWhen a message is dropped by userA to serverA, it'll drop that message to redis.\nRedis sees, who's subscribed to the topic, and sends them the message.\n\n                          Limitations\n                          --------------\n                          - Redis pubsub offers, atmost once delivery of messages, \n                            which is pretty bad, but is ok  for us, since we already have a \n                            fault tolerant mechanism in the Inbox table.\n                          \n                          - Since the Redis is part of the data plane, it needs to scale and\nhandle the distributed traffic. Now, as redis scales, each of the chat server needs to have\nconnection with every redis server (NXM connections).\nIn this case, the redis cluster is not doing a lot, just passing along messageIds. \nIf the system scales to trillions of users, it might become an issue for us, since the numbers of\nconnections to explode.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
